    "created_at": "2016-05-04T18:28:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-04T18:28:04Z",
    "body": "This is one of the items in https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/17 which attempts to align on `<code>Document</code>`.\n\nI don't think changing all our links to go to DOM makes very much sense. _Maybe_ when talking about the tree concept, but most of the time we're talking about the object in ways that are mostly defined in HTML.\n\nI actually don't have a problem with the spec's current mismash. E.g. it would be IMO weird to change from \"inserted into a document\" to \"inserted into a `Document`\". To say nothing of \"Conforming `Document`s\" or \"HTML `Document`s\". But it would also be wrong to change \"strong reference from a `Window` object to its `Document` object\" to \"strong reference from a `Window` object to its document,\" IMO.\n\nIf we see anything particularly bad we can clean it up as we go, but I don't think this is causing any confusion currently, and any changes here would as far as I can see only increase confusion.\n",
